+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Fused split-I MoE for 9 <= T <= 32 (hypothesis cuda-fused-split-i-moe-midt-cluster-reduce, rewrite stage 1).
+#
+# One own load_inline module (muse_moe_w4a16_fsi_midt_v1*): fsi_midt_kernel<NT, CL>, a persistent warp-specialized
+# Hopper kernel (producer warpgroup + two consumer warpgroups, swap-AB wgmma m64n32k16 with the dequantized NVFP4
+# weight rows as register A, as the wgmma module above) that, per (active expert, chunk of KC = 64 NT intermediate
+# columns), computes h = silu(gate) * up over the full K = 4096 for all <= 32 routes of the expert, keeps h in shared
+# memory as bf16, streams W2[:, chunk] and adds its fp32 partial y. The CL = 4 CTAs of a thread-block cluster take 4
+# adjacent chunks of the SAME expert and reduce their partial tiles through distributed shared memory before one
+# global fp32 add per row; CL = 1 is the same kernel with a plain per-CTA reduction (diagnostic and fallback). It
+# reads the wgmma module's lossless retiling of the same NVFP4 bytes (state['wg_banks']); tokens are gathered into
+# 32-row blocks by master's _align_small at block_size_m 32 (one block per active expert) and an own gather kernel.
+# A Triton combine (fp32 y32 rows, master's post-norm formula, zero-after-read) turns y32 into the bf16 output.
+#
+# Everything is prepare-gated per T class ({9..16}, {17..32}) with its own state flag state['fsi_sel'][cls] (None =
+# master's exact path): build, canary, correctness against an fp32-dequant reference, two interleaved cold-L2 graph
+# rounds against master's ACTUALLY ROUTED path on a judge-like and a random-local routing, a three-state graph copy
+# check. T <= 8 and T >= 33 never reach it.
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
